{{also|ass backwards}}
==English==
===Etymology===
US American, 1930s (Robert Whitcomb, ''Talk United States!'', p. 145).

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|alternative spelling}} [[ass backwards]], [[ass-backward]], [[ass backward]]
* {{l|en|back-asswards}}, {{l|en|bass-ackwards}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} Oriented [[backwards]], particularly after a [[mishap]].
#: ''The car spun out of control and I ended up '''ass-backwards''' in a ditch.''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|colloquial}} Hopelessly [[misguided]]; having taken the utterly wrong choice.
#: ''No wonder it doesn't work. The whole design is '''ass-backwards'''.''

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} Moving backwards, that is, [[rear end]] first.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|colloquial}} In a hopelessly misguided manner.
#: ''They did the whole design '''ass-backwards'''. No wonder it doesn't work.''

